; link_tx_10.pio; DSPi audio link NRZ transmitter, class L2, 30.72 MBd (SYS2 2.6)
;
; One instruction: one line bit every 10 sys cycles at clock divider 1.0
; (307.2 MHz / 10). The encoder packs 10-bit 8b/10b symbols MSB first into
; 32-bit words (symbol bit 'a' is the first on the wire); every link's DMA
; channel reads the same word ring, so all links of a star emit identical
; bits on identical cycles once started with pio_enable_sm_mask_in_sync().
;
; Setup: out pins = the TX GPIO (count 1), OUT shift left, autopull 32,
; TX FIFO join, clkdiv 1.0, pio_gpio_init on the pin, pindir out. Autopull
; refills the OSR in the same cycle as the out, so the bit period stays
; exactly 10 cycles as long as the TX FIFO never runs dry; an empty FIFO
; stalls the out and stretches the current bit (a receiver bit slip), so the
; encoder must stay ahead of the DMA read pointer.
;
; tools/link_rx_test models this program cycle by cycle.

.program link_tx_10
.wrap_target
    out pins, 1 [9]
.wrap
